<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib1ceba30a33765a44cf46eb9e03d609b72d8349d" commit="795c2825f0205bd7c14dc0ce1716d453ab30dfbe" commit_message="UPSTREAM: net: Clone skb before setting peeked flag  Shared skbs must not be modified and this is crucial for broadcast and/or multicast paths where we use it as an optimisation to avoid unnecessary cloning.  The function skb_recv_datagram breaks this rule by setting peeked without cloning the skb first.  This causes funky races which leads to double-free.  This patch fixes this by cloning the skb and replacing the skb in the list when setting skb-&gt;peeked.  Fixes: a59322be07c9 (&quot;[UDP]: Only increment counter on first peek/recv&quot;) Reported-by: Konstantin Khlebnikov &lt;khlebnikov@yandex-team.ru&gt; Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu &lt;herbert@gondor.apana.org.au&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit 738ac1ebb96d02e0d23bc320302a6ea94c612dec)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52665 TEST=Run suspend_stress_test on oak/elm and make sure there's no      memory corruption.  Change-Id: Ib1ceba30a33765a44cf46eb9e03d609b72d8349d Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344623 Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344623" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/23/344623/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8d21876441e25e07fef87b1a614ea051117d6b38" commit="18e42ef4ac305397595f05cb69bbe8a7718636ff" commit_message="UPSTREAM: net: Fix skb csum races when peeking  When we calculate the checksum on the recv path, we store the result in the skb as an optimisation in case we need the checksum again down the line.  This is in fact bogus for the MSG_PEEK case as this is done without any locking.  So multiple threads can peek and then store the result to the same skb, potentially resulting in bogus skb states.  This patch fixes this by only storing the result if the skb is not shared.  This preserves the optimisations for the few cases where it can be done safely due to locking or other reasons, e.g., SIOCINQ.  Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu &lt;herbert@gondor.apana.org.au&gt; Acked-by: Eric Dumazet &lt;edumazet@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit 89c22d8c3b278212eef6a8cc66b570bc840a6f5a)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52665 TEST=Run suspend_stress_test on oak/elm and make sure there's no      memory corruption.  Change-Id: I8d21876441e25e07fef87b1a614ea051117d6b38 Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344624 Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344624" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/24/344624/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I4b622d1ce724775d0a31fc5ab87b4e23e65ab584" commit="0f6c8e1b469b67baedc0ab52bae5bafb987e57e1" commit_message="UPSTREAM: net: Fix skb_set_peeked use-after-free bug  The commit 738ac1ebb96d02e0d23bc320302a6ea94c612dec (&quot;net: Clone skb before setting peeked flag&quot;) introduced a use-after-free bug in skb_recv_datagram.  This is because skb_set_peeked may create a new skb and free the existing one.  As it stands the caller will continue to use the old freed skb.  This patch fixes it by making skb_set_peeked return the new skb (or the old one if unchanged).  Fixes: 738ac1ebb96d (&quot;net: Clone skb before setting peeked flag&quot;) Reported-by: Brenden Blanco &lt;bblanco@plumgrid.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu &lt;herbert@gondor.apana.org.au&gt; Tested-by: Brenden Blanco &lt;bblanco@plumgrid.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Konstantin Khlebnikov &lt;khlebnikov@yandex-team.ru&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit a0a2a6602496a45ae838a96db8b8173794b5d398)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52665 TEST=Run suspend_stress_test on oak/elm and make sure there's no      memory corruption.  Change-Id: I4b622d1ce724775d0a31fc5ab87b4e23e65ab584 Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344625 Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344625" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/25/344625/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I61a9b32a0178fde2bc9ba0d4f66a8e6c7e065501" commit="12d12275121c6c0b523579f1c710dd12b1a14dc4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: core: enable more fine-grained datagram reception control  The __skb_recv_datagram routine in core/ datagram.c provides a general skb reception factility supposed to be utilized by protocol modules providing datagram sockets. It encompasses both the actual recvmsg code and a surrounding 'sleep until data is available' loop. This is inconvenient if a protocol module has to use additional locking in order to maintain some per-socket state the generic datagram socket code is unaware of (as the af_unix code does). The patch below moves the recvmsg proper code into a new __skb_try_recv_datagram routine which doesn't sleep and renames wait_for_more_packets to __skb_wait_for_more_packets, both routines being exported interfaces. The original __skb_recv_datagram routine is reimplemented on top of these two functions such that its user-visible behaviour remains unchanged.  Signed-off-by: Rainer Weikusat &lt;rweikusat@mobileactivedefense.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit ea3793ee29d3621faf857fa8ef5425e9ff9a756d)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52665 TEST=Run suspend_stress_test on oak/elm and make sure there's no      memory corruption.  Change-Id: I61a9b32a0178fde2bc9ba0d4f66a8e6c7e065501 Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344626 Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344626" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/26/344626/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6736b6b60b316879bea08249e3edaceb54f73c46" commit="c0668ee674bbd388478317c896fd0b3e3e95051c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: net: Fix inverted test in __skb_recv_datagram  As the kernel generally uses negated error numbers, *err needs to be compared with -EAGAIN (d'oh).  Signed-off-by: Rainer Weikusat &lt;rweikusat@mobileactivedefense.com&gt; Fixes: ea3793ee29d3 (&quot;core: enable more fine-grained datagram reception control&quot;) Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit 760a4322470e3990b14e09bfe80c9c75c77f33dd)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52665 TEST=Run suspend_stress_test on oak/elm and make sure there's no      memory corruption.  Change-Id: I6736b6b60b316879bea08249e3edaceb54f73c46 Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344627 Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344627" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/27/344627/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6b1af008df4fa283b9a1d1e942c353a0e5241135" commit="8f178f8cf927642bf10a41216c08e99298db0a09" commit_message="env.paths: move path functions from test.factory  Refactor path-related functions and constants.  Retain aliases in test.factory for backwards compatibility.  from:   cros.factory.test.factory into:   cros.factory.test.env.paths  moved:   get_factory_root()   get_log_root()   get_state_root()   get_test_data_root()   CONSOLE_LOG_PATH --&gt; GetConsoleLogPath()   FACTORY_LOG_PATH --&gt; GetFactoryLogPath()   FACTORY_LOG_PATH_ON_DEVICE  BUG=None TEST=Run test suite  Change-Id: I6b1af008df4fa283b9a1d1e942c353a0e5241135 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/343539 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="343539" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/39/343539/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic6ea9086fc4254e611d6e39fe560e9e7cb0aa308" commit="dcb99e16542566dfc0969afcc0ff3b4727d4bb20" commit_message="testlog: add support for python logging  Add support for Python logging calls.  Calls to logging (info, debug, exception, etc.)  will be created as testlog objects and saved to disk as JSON.  BUG=chromium:609069 TEST=Manually on DUT CQ-DEPEND=CL:343539  Change-Id: Ic6ea9086fc4254e611d6e39fe560e9e7cb0aa308 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341894 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="341894" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="15" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/94/341894/15" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6ba93c3503100b06c0cea18424ad44750130b45c" commit="6f78024ec6cc2b938e0bdccf30bb5d59a6815450" commit_message="testlog: add support for test_run event  Add initial support for test_run event according to its specification in the Testlog API Playbook.  More fields will be added later.  BUG=chromium:609069 TEST=Manually on DUT  Change-Id: I6ba93c3503100b06c0cea18424ad44750130b45c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342327 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342327" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/27/342327/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I32e569c5fdf5dab9aad6ac485e301a2133bd8a2e" commit="751c05156c9008a4e6135ccd9b1f21506f48a9d3" commit_message="invocation: change end_time to object member  Rename end_time to TestInvocation object variable self.end_time, in preparation for end_time being used in testlog event emitting.  BUG=chromium:609069 TEST=Manually on DUT  Change-Id: I32e569c5fdf5dab9aad6ac485e301a2133bd8a2e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342328 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342328" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" pa