0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/64/344564/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2606f14cb112c760c1857a1e6f288985616bb0e0" commit="3dd0a2432b5beb795f3b9fd993369b00a2bc9e2d" commit_message="inform_shopfloor: remove waiting for interface ready  Previously we will wait for interface ready before posting. However, different board may have different interface name, e.g. eth0, wan0, making it difficult to check the correct one. This check can be removed. The posting can be retried to avoid the problem.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I2606f14cb112c760c1857a1e6f288985616bb0e0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344473 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="344473" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/memento_softwareupdate" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/memento_softwareupdate" ref="refs/changes/73/344473/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8345fdf7d20203ca8b14e5498707cb5328aebc1a" commit="5d23bb1fd7b5be92984599ea9933e3c0705613e0" commit_message="[autotest] audio_AlsaAPI: Add the test for ALSA API  Wraps alsa_api_test binary to test ALSA API including these: - drop: Test snd_pcm_drop can drop playback and reset hw_ptr. It fails   on some boards where drop is implemented as pause. - fill: Test filling buffer get from snd_pcm_mmap_begin. - move: Test snd_pcm_forward can move appl_ptr to the front of hw_ptr.  BUG=chromium:601346 TEST=run audio_AlsaAPI test on samus. Fill and move pass while drop fails.  Change-Id: I8345fdf7d20203ca8b14e5498707cb5328aebc1a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/343402 Commit-Ready: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="343402" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/02/343402/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iacf0df60ca890f9ccd84f149c9b3f9283420d3b2" commit="73e94821e73ecef506ee0c9c3199df125dd010b2" commit_message="[autotest] audio_test_utils: Ignore harmonics of frequencies to be ignored  There are non-perfect noise pattern from power noise and cause spectral energy at 60Hz, 120Hz, 180Hz. We should ignore harmonics of 60Hz when we examine the spectral.  BUG=chromium:611643 TEST=run audio_AudioBasicInternalSpeaker test on jerry on android1758-audiobox2-host1  Change-Id: Iacf0df60ca890f9ccd84f149c9b3f9283420d3b2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344565 Commit-Ready: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344565" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/65/344565/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4bf63e454afa77e6b37f9c2650377f1de3854c25" commit="809cf2a2957aec17bbbc6b510179f3b008d7a9b6" commit_message="overlord: fixture: implement group filtering and switching  Some factories may have several projects running at the same time. Add a group filter to filter between then to eliminate the need have having a second overlord instance running.  BUG=chromium:611287 TEST=manually  Change-Id: I4bf63e454afa77e6b37f9c2650377f1de3854c25 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344137 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344137" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/37/344137/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I66015157179c9ef4a0fe01fac52df9e475115777" commit="8cedf07fb3240cc9fdf8b01da803365c407fe5e0" commit_message="Add 'external' package to solve module dependency on limited environment.  When running ChromeOS factory software on non-ChromeOS environment (either on station or other systems like Android) it becomes a problem to maintain and provide external modules.  This issue was more difficult to solve when the DUT API is introduced. The DUT API itself is lazy-loaded, but its dependencies still must be imported, even if that particular module won't be used by target tests.  A possible solution is to add more try-catch when loading modules that few of our DRM (display) and camera tests already did, but that would put the dirty try-catch everywhere and is hard to maintain.  This commit provides a unified way by moving all external dependencies to cros.factory.external. All modules there act like a proxy to real external modules, and won't fail (will become empty, or alternative implementations) unless you want to debug on it (using environment variable DEBUG_IMPORT). DUT API users can even check the 'MODULE_READY' variable to see if the underlying module (or package) was properly loaded.  See py/external/README for more details.  Note 'yaml' was left unchanged because it was exactly the core of too many modules.  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I66015157179c9ef4a0fe01fac52df9e475115777 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/343615 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="343615" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="19" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/15/343615/19" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4aff61d102e22f1bcbfeda97746b67b6f2257e84" commit="c100a8d3a12e456742e07e44017bd706bad0cc03" commit_message="CRAS: bt_device - Add a delay between BT profile switch  According to our test so far, there are two BT audio device fail to output any sound after immediate switching from HFP to A2DP. The same test works fine on other operating system but having a noticible delay, detailed in the bug. This change adds a 500ms delay between the BT profile switching to improve the user experience on certain BT devices. During that 500ms period of time, audio samples will be written to the silent device in CRAS, which is considered acceptable since switching from HFP to A2DP already introduces observable gap, and the final measured gap time is shorter than on other operating system.  BUG=chromium:558667 TEST=Test BT profile switching on UE Mini Boom speaker and Sony SBH54 headset.  Change-Id: I4aff61d102e22f1bcbfeda97746b67b6f2257e84 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344123 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="344123" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/23/344123/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><lkgm version="8328.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>